N5008 [temp.alias]/2, [temp.spec.partial.match]/1, [temp.deduct.type]/8:
the partial specialization pattern `A<ident<volatile T, int>>' is
`A<volatile T>' and matches A<volatile tup> with T = tup; likewise for
`const volatile T'.  Through the alias the front end matches the const
pattern only; a volatile or const volatile argument selects the primary
template (the same patterns written without the alias work).  libc++'s
cv-qualified tuple_size specializations are written exactly this way
(__enable_if_tuple_size_imp<volatile _Tp, ...>), so tuple_size<volatile
tuple<...>> has no value.  Found while writing
cpp17_tuple_size_selected_despite_cv_partial_specializations.  g++ 13 and
clang++ 18 accept the program.  Pre-existing (fails on bin52).
